Cell operations (design 3.6 - 3.8), styles and cell properties.

=== divide at the caret
--- before
#% cell
ab▮cd
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+D
--- after
#% cell
ab

#% cell
▮cd

=== divide at a line start drops the line break
--- before
#% cell
a = 1
▮b = 2
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+D
--- after
#% cell
a = 1

#% cell
▮b = 2

=== divide with a selection makes up to three cells
--- before
#% text
# ab⟦cd⟧ef
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+D
--- after
#% text
# ab

#% text
# ▮cd

#% text
# ef

=== a divided input loses its label
--- before
#% cell label=4
x▮y
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+D
--- after
#% cell
x

#% cell
▮y

=== merge joins the cells into the first one's style
--- before
#% cell
a=1

#% cell
b=2

#% text
# c
--- keys
Bracket(0) Shift+Bracket(2) Ctrl+Shift+M
--- after
#% cell ◆
a=1
b=2
c

=== merge drops generated cells
--- before
#% cell label=1
1
#% output n=1
#= 1

#% cell
2
--- keys
Bracket(0) Shift+Bracket(2) Ctrl+Shift+M
--- after
#% cell label=1 ◆
1
2

=== merging one cell does nothing
--- before
#% cell ◆
a
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+M
--- after
#% cell ◆
a

=== input from above
--- before
#% cell
f(x)

#% text
# t
‖
--- keys
Ctrl+L
--- after
#% cell
f(x)

#% text
# t

#% cell
f(x)▮

=== output from above makes an input
--- before
#% cell label=1
1+1
#% output n=1
#= 2
‖
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+L
--- after
#% cell label=1
1+1
#% output n=1
#= 2

#% cell
2▮

=== same style below goes directly after the cell, before its outputs
--- before
#% cell label=1
x▮
#% output n=1
#= x
--- keys
Alt+Enter "y"
--- after
#% cell label=1
x

#% cell
y▮
#% output n=1
#= x
--- groups
x {y x}

=== same style below in text
--- before
#% text
# a▮
--- keys
Alt+Enter "b"
--- after
#% text
# a

#% text
# b▮

=== Alt+digit sets the style of the caret's cell
--- before
#% text
# Heading▮
--- keys
Alt+4
--- after
#% section
# Heading▮

=== a style without labels drops the label
--- before
#% cell label=2
x▮
--- keys
Alt+7
--- after
#% text
# x▮

=== Ctrl+8 toggles the initialization attribute
--- before
#% cell
x▮

#% code
y
--- keys
Ctrl+8 Down Down Ctrl+8
--- after
#% cell init
x

#% code noinit
y▮

=== show expression shows the cell's source; edited and shown again it reads back
--- before
#% cell label=2
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+E Click(0,15) " noeval" Ctrl+Shift+E
--- after
#% cell label=2 noeval ◆
x

=== a cell shown as its source is saved as the cell it describes
--- before
#% text
# hello▮
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+E
--- after
#% text ◆
# hello

=== Delete with cells selected deletes them
--- before
#% cell
a

#% cell
b

#% cell
c
--- keys
Bracket(1) Delete
--- after
#% cell
a

‖
#% cell
c

=== cells that cannot be deleted stay
--- before
#% cell nodelete
a
--- keys
Bracket(0) Delete
--- after
#% cell nodelete ◆
a

=== copy and paste cells at an insertion point
--- before
#% cell label=1
a
#% output n=1
#= a

#% text
# t
--- keys
Bracket(0,2) Ctrl+C Gap(3) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell label=1
a
#% output n=1
#= a

#% text
# t

#% cell label=1
a
#% output n=1
#= a
‖

=== plain text pasted at an insertion point becomes one input cell
--- before
‖
--- keys
Clip("x = 1\ny = 2") Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell
x = 1
y = 2▮

=== text pasted into a cell replaces the selection
--- before
#% cell
a⟦b⟧c
--- keys
Clip("XY") Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell
aXY▮c

=== paste over selected cells replaces them
--- before
#% cell
a

#% cell
b
--- keys
Clip("z") Bracket(0) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell
z▮

#% cell
b

=== cut cells, undo brings them back
--- before
#% cell
a

#% cell
b
--- keys
Bracket(0) Ctrl+X Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell ◆
a

#% cell
b

=== move cells by dragging their bracket
--- before
#% text
# a

#% text
# b

#% text
# c
--- keys
Bracket(0) Move(3)
--- after
#% text
# b

#% text
# c

#% text ◆
# a

=== copy cells by dragging with Ctrl
--- before
#% text
# a

#% text
# b
--- keys
Bracket(0) CopyTo(2)
--- after
#% text
# a

#% text
# b

#% text ◆
# a

=== shift-click extends a cell selection; ctrl-click toggles one cell
--- before
#% text
# a

#% text
# b

#% text
# c

#% text
# d
--- keys
Bracket(0) Shift+Bracket(2) Ctrl+Bracket(1)
--- after
#% text ◆
# a

#% text
# b

#% text ◆
# c

#% text
# d

=== undo of a merge restores the cells
--- before
#% cell
a

#% cell
b
--- keys
Bracket(0) Shift+Bracket(1) Ctrl+Shift+M Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell ◆
a

#% cell ◆
b
